# DeviceFrame - a device around a picture of a product: a phone (rounded bezel) or a browser window (a bar with
# three dots). Put an Image, or any content, in the slot; an Image fills the screen from the top. height crops it
# (the rest fades out at the bottom), so a tall screenshot can sit beside a short text.
#   DeviceFrame { Image "~/shots/store.png" alt("Tu tienda en un teléfono") }
#   DeviceFrame(kind: "browser", height: "420px") { Image "~/shots/panel.png" alt("Tu panel") }
# width: empty (a phone is 280 px, a browser fills its column) or a width like «320px».
# kind: phone | browser. shadcn-for-muten · part · no deps · kit.css (.cx-device).
part DeviceFrame(kind: text = "phone", height: text = "", width: text = "") { Stack class("cx-device") data(kind: $kind, crop: $height != "", sized: $width != "") style(h: "{$height}", w: "{$width}") { slot } }
